    <statement><p>Find the equation of the sphere centered at <m>(2, 5, -5)</m> with
radius 6.  Normalize your equations so that the coefficient of
<m>x^2</m> is 1.</p>
<p><fillin characters="60" name="AnSwEr0001"/> = 0.</p>
<p>Give an equation which describes the intersection of this sphere with
the plane <m>z = -4</m>.</p>
<p><fillin characters="60" name="AnSwEr0002"/> = 0.</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\left(x-2\right)^{2}+\left(y-5\right)^{2}+\left(z-\left(-5\right)\right)^{2}-36</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\left(x-2\right)^{2}+\left(y-5\right)^{2}+1-36</m>
      </p>
